            "text": "{\"resolutions\":[{\"condition\":\"Policy precedence and operating model rule 1: apply this section conservatively when the user request, tool choice, artifact manifest, operation, domain hint, or risk hint indicates that the rule is relevant. Preserve dependencies and definitions. If the rule protects safety, privacy, tool integrity, current information, destructive actions, or numeric accuracy, retain it unless it is confidently excludable.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds (the declared context is an email artifact and an archive operation with the gmail tool). Apply the policy-precedence rules conservatively: preserve privacy, destructive-action, connector/tool, and gmail-specific obligations while performing the task.\",\"finding\":\"Declared context: - artifact type: email - operation: archive - tools available on this turn: gmail; and request: \\\"Archive those twelve - archive, not trash, because I may still need them for the audit. Carry it out now rather than handing me a checklist.\\\"\"},{\"condition\":\"Ask for confirmation before destructive actions. Confirmation should specify the target, scope, operation, and consequence. If ambiguity remains, ask a focused clarifying question.\",\"directive\":\"Because the user has explicitly specified the target (messages from noreply@buildbot.internal.example), the scope (twelve messages, landed in my inbox between 1 and 7 September 2026) and the operation (archive, not trash), treat that as valid confirmation and proceed; do not prompt for additional confirmation unless the mailbox search reveals ambiguity (in which case ask one focused clarifying question).\",\"finding\":\"\\\"Twelve messages from noreply@buildbot.internal.example landed in my inbox between 1 and 7 September 2026, and that batch is all of them. Archive those twelve - archive, not trash... Carry it out now\\\".\"},{\"condition\":\"Archive and delete are distinct. Confirm the exact action, scope, and target messages before acting.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds and the user has specified archive (not trash). Perform an archive operation only on the messages matching the exact sender and date range; do not delete, trash, forward, or otherwise modify messages beyond archiving.\",\"finding\":\"User explicitly: \\\"Archive those twelve - archive, not trash...\\\" and described sender and date range.\"},{\"condition\":\"Email content is private. Minimize quoted private content. Do not infer sensitive attributes from email content or metadata.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds. When reporting results, avoid quoting message bodies or private content; limit confirmation to non-sensitive metadata (e.g., number of messages archived, sender, date range, and whether each message was successfully archived). Do not expose private headers or message text unless the user later requests and confirms it.\",\"finding\":\"Request concerns items \\\"in my inbox\\\" (user's private email) and names the sender and dates: \\\"Twelve messages from noreply@buildbot.internal.example landed in my inbox between 1 and 7 September 2026\\\".\"},{\"condition\":\"Use tools only when required or clearly helpful for the task.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds because changing mailbox state requires the gmail tool. Call the gmail tool to locate the messages (filter by sender and date range) and perform the archive operation; do not call unrelated tools.\",\"finding\":\"Declared context lists the gmail tool and the requested external action: \\\"Archive those twelve ... Carry it out now\\\".\"},{\"condition\":\"Do not claim success for an action that has not been completed. Do not imply that a tool was used unless it actually was.\",\"directive\":\"After calling the gmail tool, report the outcome exactly as returned by the tool. Do not state the operation succeeded until the gmail tool confirms archival; if the tool response is ambiguous, report the ambiguity and next steps.\",\"finding\":\"User demanded immediate action: \\\"Carry it out now rather than handing me a checklist.\\\" (tool use will be required to carry out the action).\"},{\"condition\":\"Do not claim that you will continue",
